================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

Every dependency in this workspace is permissively licensed; there is no
copyleft anywhere in the tree. `cargo deny check` enforces that against the
allow-list in `deny.toml`.

Most dependencies are MIT OR Apache-2.0 and are satisfied by the MIT notice
above. The four below carry terms that travel with a BINARY and are therefore
reproduced or pointed to explicitly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ring — Apache-2.0 AND ISC
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
https://github.com/briansmith/ring

`ring` is dual-natured: its own code is ISC-style, and it incorporates code
derived from BoringSSL (Apache-2.0, Copyright The BoringSSL Authors / Google
Inc.) and from fiat-crypto (MIT, Copyright the fiat-crypto authors). Both
upstream notices are carried in `ring`'s own LICENSE file, which a distribution
of this software in binary form must include.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
unicode-ident — (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
https://github.com/dtolnay/unicode-ident

The Unicode-3.0 arm is NOT optional — it applies in addition to the MIT/Apache
choice, because the crate embeds data tables derived from the Unicode Character
Database. The Unicode, Inc. license agreement for data files and software
applies to those tables.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
arrayref — BSD-2-Clause
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
https://github.com/droundy/arrayref

Copyright (c) 2015 David Roundy. Redistribution in binary form must reproduce
the BSD-2-Clause notice and disclaimer in the documentation or other materials
provided with the distribution.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mimalloc — MIT  (x86_64-unknown-linux-musl builds ONLY)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
https://github.com/microsoft/mimalloc

Copyright (c) 2018-2021 Microsoft Corporation, Daan Leijen. The Rust binding
vendors mimalloc's C sources.

This dependency is **target-conditional**: it is compiled only for musl targets,
where the single-arena system allocator serialises concurrent allocation-heavy
queries. A build for any other target does not include it.

That is why per-target notices matter here, and why the release job emits
`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-<triple>.txt` rather than one file: a notice listing
mimalloc for a glibc build would be claiming a component that is not in it, and
one omitting it for a musl build would be missing a component that is.

